From: PowOS <noreply@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: popups of a task's window stay inside the task

A window shown as its own Android task (0013) draws only what lies inside the task: its client area at the task's
size. Its popups - menus, combo boxes, tooltips (xdg_popup) - were placed by their positioner against the output's
placement area, so a menu that ran past the window's edge was cut off by the task (Kate's menus in a floating window
on the unfolded home).

Workspace::setPopupAreaHandler(): the platform may give a parent window's popups a smaller area to be placed in;
XdgPopupWindow::updateRelativePlacement() uses it instead of the output's area, so the positioner's own constraint
adjustment (flip, slide, resize) keeps the popup inside it, as on a small screen. The anland backend gives the task's
area (AnlandWindowTask::area) for a window shown in a task, its dialogs (drawn into the same task) and their popups;
every other window - the desktop's, in the Plasma app - keeps the output's area, so KWin's own popups are unchanged.
---

--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
@@ -486,6 +486,18 @@ RectF AnlandWindowTask::viewport() const
     return RectF(client.topLeft(), size);
 }
 
+RectF AnlandWindowTask::area() const
+{
+    if (!m_window) {
+        return RectF();
+    }
+    const RectF client = m_window->clientGeometry();
+    if (fitsWindow() || taskSize().isEmpty()) {
+        return client;
+    }
+    return RectF(client.topLeft(), QSizeF(taskSize()) / scale());
+}
+
 QSize AnlandWindowTask::taskSize() const
 {
     // Never past the buffers: what doesn't fit them can't be shown.
@@ -991,6 +1003,18 @@ void AnlandWindowTasks::integrate()
         }
         return show(window);
     });
+    // A popup (menu, combo box, tooltip) of a window shown in a task - or of its dialog, which the task draws too
+    // (attach) - is placed inside the task, which shows nothing beyond it: placed against the output, Kate's menus
+    // ran past the window and were cut off. The desktop's windows keep the output's area (their popups are KWin's own).
+    workspace()->setPopupAreaHandler([this](const Window *parent) -> std::optional<RectF> {
+        for (const Window *w = parent; w; w = w->transientFor()) {
+            if (AnlandWindowTask *task = taskFor(w)) {
+                const RectF area = task->area();
+                return area.isEmpty() ? std::nullopt : std::optional<RectF>(area);
+            }
+        }
+        return std::nullopt;
+    });
     // An application going full screen (a game, Steam Big Picture, a video) gets its own task the same way, shown
     // immersive; leaving full screen gives it back.
     for (Window *window : workspace()->windows()) {
@@ -1225,7 +1249,7 @@ bool AnlandWindowTasks::exportable(Window *window) const
         && window->desktopFileName() != QLatin1String("org.kde.plasmashell");
 }
 
-AnlandWindowTask *AnlandWindowTasks::taskFor(Window *window) const
+AnlandWindowTask *AnlandWindowTasks::taskFor(const Window *window) const
 {
     for (AnlandWindowTask *task : m_tasks) {
         if (window && task->window() == window) {

